        <rdfs:label>pole bud</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00000091"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Cytoplasmic bud that forms at the posterior pole of the embryo during cycle 9. Pole buds give rise to the pole cells.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0064779</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00000092 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00000092">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00004860"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002202"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00053322"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002292"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://flybase.org/reports/FBgn0283442"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Cell that begins as a pole cell, becomes incorporated into the gonad and can develop into a germline stem cell (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; Dansereau and Lasko, 2008; Slaidina et al., 2020).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/696</obo:IAO_0000233>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>GC</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CL:0000301</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PGC</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pole cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00000092</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#FB_gloss"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Can be identified in the larva by expression of vasa (Slaidina et al., 2020). Only a small subset of pole cells can become germ cells and this fate might be specified by the time the posterior midgut primordium invaginates (Okada, 1998).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>primordial germ cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00000092"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Cell that begins as a pole cell, becomes incorporated into the gonad and can develop into a germline stem cell (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997; Dansereau and Lasko, 2008; Slaidina et al., 2020).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0089570</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0101973</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0216027</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0244767</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
