        <obo:IAO_0000115>Larval segmental nerve of a larval abdominal segment. These are only found in segments A1-7, as A8 and A9 do not have separate segmental and intersegmental nerves (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It has two roots, anterior and posterior, both formed from neurons of the same segment as the nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Proximally it shares a glial sheath with the intersegmental nerve before branching from it at the ventral edge of the ventral oblique muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). A thick, posteriorly directed branch (SNc) leaves the main trunk of the nerve (SNa) and splits into fine branches - 3 carrying axons from the ventral sensory cluster and a 4th carrying efferents to the ventral acute musculature (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The SNa branch continues dorsally and carries efferent axons innervating the external lateral transverse and lateral oblique muscles and the axons of v&apos;es2 and v&apos;ch1 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1565</obo:IAO_0000233>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>FBbt:00002450</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00002197</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>larval abdominal SN</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>larval abdominal posterior fascicle</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>larval segmental nerve of A1-7</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00002197</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:label>larval abdominal segmental nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002197"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Larval segmental nerve of a larval abdominal segment. These are only found in segments A1-7, as A8 and A9 do not have separate segmental and intersegmental nerves (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It has two roots, anterior and posterior, both formed from neurons of the same segment as the nerve (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Proximally it shares a glial sheath with the intersegmental nerve before branching from it at the ventral edge of the ventral oblique muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). A thick, posteriorly directed branch (SNc) leaves the main trunk of the nerve (SNa) and splits into fine branches - 3 carrying axons from the ventral sensory cluster and a 4th carrying efferents to the ventral acute musculature (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The SNa branch continues dorsally and carries efferent axons innervating the external lateral transverse and lateral oblique muscles and the axons of v&apos;es2 and v&apos;ch1 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).</owl:annotatedTarget>
