    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00003668 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00003668">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00040007"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00003632"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002202"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00111206"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A handle bar-shaped synaptic neuropil located just posterior to the fan-shaped body. Its lateral edge ends at the posterior end of the inferior clamp (ICL) near the medial equatorial fascicle (MEF). A row of 18 connected slices (9 on each side of the midline, numbered 1-9 from medial to lateral) that forms a dorso-posteriorly located part of the central complex embedded in the cortex between the calyces of the two mushroom bodies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00003668</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PB</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PCB</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00003668</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#BrainName"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The identification of the most medial slice (slice 1) by Wolff et al. (2015) meant that the domain that was previously called slice 1 corresponds in fact to slice 2. Each of the two neighboring slices (2-3, 4-5, 6-7, 8-9) are associated more closely because small-field columnar neurons innervate the fan-shaped body via the protocerebral bridge, and these neurons are generated by the same neuroblasts, forming four groups on each side of the midline, from lateral to medial: segment pair W, X, Y and Z (Boyan and Williams et al., 2011; Ito and Awasaki, 2008).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>protocerebral bridge</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction>https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/f073/4407839/e48065582b72/cne0523-0997-f1.jpg</foaf:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00003668"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A handle bar-shaped synaptic neuropil located just posterior to the fan-shaped body. Its lateral edge ends at the posterior end of the inferior clamp (ICL) near the medial equatorial fascicle (MEF). A row of 18 connected slices (9 on each side of the midline, numbered 1-9 from medial to lateral) that forms a dorso-posteriorly located part of the central complex embedded in the cortex between the calyces of the two mushroom bodies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0049409</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0205148</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
