        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Spine shaped gustatory bristle, between 12-45 micrometres long, found on the prothoracic (1st) leg of the adult. There are approximately 37 of these bristles per female prothoracic leg, and 50 per male prothoracic leg (Stocker, 1994).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0049501</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
