        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058207"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe. The majority of the local interneurons of the adult antennal lobe fall into this class.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-12-14T01:45:23Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00007402</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>GABAergic adult AL LN</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00007402</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Based on GABA expression, approximately 80% of the local interneurons of the adult antennal lobe are GABAergic (Wilson and Laurent, 2005). Tanaka et al (2012) distinguishes two different types: LN1 and LN2L. LN1 neurons arborize in most of the glomeruli, whereas LN2L neurons are much more diverse.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe. The majority of the local interneurons of the adult antennal lobe fall into this class.</owl:annotatedTarget>
