        <obo:IAO_0000115>Diploid endocrine cell which is part of the adult midgut epithelium. There are approximately 1100 of these cells in an adult midgut (Chen et al., 2016). They develop from enteroendocrine precursor cells (Chen et al., 2018).</obo:IAO_0000115>
