        <obo:IAO_0000115>Adult dopaminergic neuron with its cell body in the gnathal ganglion (Marella et al., 2012). The ventral gnathal ganglion has four dopaminergic neurons; a bilateral pair with each neuron arborizing in one half of the subesophageal zone, a relatively anterior unpaired neuron and a relatively posterior unpaired neuron (Marella et al., 2012).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-26T14:06:48Z</dc:date>
