                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00003624"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mechanosensory neuron of the adult that innervates a scolopidium of a chordotonal organ in the leg and ascends to the brain. Different neurons reach different destinations, such as the gnathal ganglion, wedge and anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-15T09:38:51Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00048275</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Lco1N brain</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>leg chordotonal organ primary neuron of brain</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>Lco1N1B</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>Lco1N2B</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>SA_DLV</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>ascending club FeCO neuron</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>femoral chordotonal club ascending neuron</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00048275</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Ascending club neurons appear to be the only ascending leg chordotonal neurons (Lee et al., 2025 - FBrf0262248). These are SA_DLV in Codex, based on community annotations (2025-06-18).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>ascending mechanosensory neuron of leg chordotonal organ</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
