        <owl:annotatedTarget>Adult histaminergic neuron with its cell body in the mesothoracic neuromere (Nassel et al., 1990). There is one of these cells on each side and its soma is located ventrally (Nassel et al., 1990). It has an axon that runs dorsally and anteriorly, entering the cervical connective (Nassel et al., 1990; Cheong et al., 2024). It arborizes bilaterally in the ventral nerve cord and in the brain (Cheong et al., 2024). It receives most of its input in the wing neuropil and intermediate tectulum (Cheong et al., 2024). Its presynapses are found throughout the pro- and meso-thoracic neuromeres as well as in the subesophageal zone, saddle and posterior slope (Cheong et al., 2024).</owl:annotatedTarget>
