        <obo:IAO_0000115>Ensheathing glial cell of the larval brain. There are approximately 12 of these cells in each brain hemisphere throughout larval development (Omoto et al., 2015).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-10-27T10:37:47Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00052370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>embryonic/larval brain ensheathing neuropil associated glial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00052370</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval brain ensheathing glial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052370"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ensheathing glial cell of the larval brain. There are approximately 12 of these cells in each brain hemisphere throughout larval development (Omoto et al., 2015).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0229106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052371 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052371">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047836"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00001102"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047837"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047858"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Ensheathing glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. There are approximately four of these cells that ensheath the synaptic neuropil in each abdominal hemineuromere throughout larval development, including two that wrap the proximal parts of the nerve roots (Pogodalla et al., 2021). Three of these four synaptic neuropil-ensheathing glia derive from the longitudinal glioblast (Peco et al., 2016). There are also three or four midline glia per neuromere, which ensheath the commissural axons (Ito et al., 1995; Banerjee et al., 2017). Some of these cells also extend into the dorsal cell body rind and wrap neuronal cell bodies (Pogodalla et al., 2021).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-10-27T10:39:12Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00052371</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord ensheathing neuropil associated glial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00052371</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval VNC ensheathing glial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052371"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ensheathing glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. There are approximately four of these cells that ensheath the synaptic neuropil in each abdominal hemineuromere throughout larval development, including two that wrap the proximal parts of the nerve roots (Pogodalla et al., 2021). Three of these four synaptic neuropil-ensheathing glia derive from the longitudinal glioblast (Peco et al., 2016). There are also three or four midline glia per neuromere, which ensheath the commissural axons (Ito et al., 1995; Banerjee et al., 2017). Some of these cells also extend into the dorsal cell body rind and wrap neuronal cell bodies (Pogodalla et al., 2021).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0082171</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0231858</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0236333</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0251788</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052372 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052372">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100505"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00001102"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047840"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047858"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00110878"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002202"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00001311"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Astrocyte-like glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. It has a prominent process extending into the neuropil proximal to its nucleus (Pogodalla et al., 2021). There are approximately 6 of these cells in each hemineuromere throughout larval development, found in fixed locations: 3 dorsal, 2 lateral and one ventral (Peco et al., 2016). They develop from prospero-expressing interface glia (Peco et al., 2016).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-10-27T10:57:14Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00052372</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord astrocyte-like neuropil associated glial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord reticulated neuropil associated glial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00052372</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval VNC astrocyte-like glial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00052372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Astrocyte-like glial cell of the larval ventral nerve cord. It has a prominent process extending into the neuropil proximal to its nucleus (Pogodalla et al., 2021). There are approximately 6 of these cells in each hemineuromere throughout larval development, found in fixed locations: 3 dorsal, 2 lateral and one ventral (Peco et al., 2016). They develop from prospero-expressing interface glia (Peco et al., 2016).</owl:annotatedTarget>
