                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0013003"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00111268"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>Dm10</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Distal medullary wide-field amacrine neuron whose cell body is located in the cell body rind of the medulla. It has a distinct tri-stratified layer pattern, branching extensively in medulla layers M1, M3B and M5. Its arbor resembles an ellipse, with the long axis aligned with the dorsal-ventral axis, and covering less than 10 columns. The processes in M1 and M3B to M5 are located in an intracolumnar position. There are around 300 Dm10 neurons per hemisphere. They are GABAergic (Davis et al., 2020).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5948-3092"/>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-05-22T02:28:19Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00110135</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Dm1-5</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Dm10</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>distal medullary amacrine neuron Dm1-5</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00110135</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Pre-synaptic terminals were assessed by labelling with a UAS-Synaptotagmin reporter (P{UAS-HA-syt} - FBtp0015803). The identification of dendrites and axons was done using a UAS-Dscam (P{UAS-Dscam.exon17.1.GFP} - FBtp0021447) or a UAS-tau (P{SUAS-tau-lacZ.O} - FBtp0010033) reporter, respectively (Morante and Desplan, 2008).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>distal medullary amacrine neuron Dm10</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
