    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005304 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005304">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005259"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00018001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005289"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005290"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005301"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Stage during which most of the nuclei are arranged as a monolayer at the cortex (periphery) of the embryo (Foe and Alberts, 1983; Jaeger et al., 2012). It begins shortly after completion of the ninth cleavage division and lasts until the onset of gastrulation, including cleavage cycles 10-14A  (Foe and Alberts, 1983; Jaeger et al., 2012). This corresponds to embryonic stages 4 (syncitial blastoderm stage) and 5 (cellular blastoderm stage) (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>blastoderm</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>FlyBase_development_CV</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBdv:00005304</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Temporal ordering number - 160.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>blastoderm stage</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005304"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Stage during which most of the nuclei are arranged as a monolayer at the cortex (periphery) of the embryo (Foe and Alberts, 1983; Jaeger et al., 2012). It begins shortly after completion of the ninth cleavage division and lasts until the onset of gastrulation, including cleavage cycles 10-14A  (Foe and Alberts, 1983; Jaeger et al., 2012). This corresponds to embryonic stages 4 (syncitial blastoderm stage) and 5 (cellular blastoderm stage) (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0039741</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0089570</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0220623</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


