                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005304"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005311"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Stage during which gastrulation occurs. During this stage, cells from the polar caps and the mid-ventral part of the blastoderm invaginate and ultimately generate the germ layers (Hartenstein, 1993). This encompasses embryonic stages 6-8 (Hartenstein, 1993).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>gastrula</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>gastrulation stage</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>FlyBase_development_CV</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBdv:00005317</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Temporal ordering number - 220.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>gastrula stage</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005317"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Stage during which gastrulation occurs. During this stage, cells from the polar caps and the mid-ventral part of the blastoderm invaginate and ultimately generate the germ layers (Hartenstein, 1993). This encompasses embryonic stages 6-8 (Hartenstein, 1993).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0064803</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005318 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005318">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005259"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00018001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005317"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005304"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005311"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Stage 6 begins when the ventral furrow becomes apparent, an event which is followed rapidly by the formation of the cephalic furrow. Stage 6 ends when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (170-180 minutes after egg laying).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>FlyBase_development_CV</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBdv:00005318</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Temporal ordering number - 230.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>embryonic stage 6</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005318"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Stage 6 begins when the ventral furrow becomes apparent, an event which is followed rapidly by the formation of the cephalic furrow. Stage 6 ends when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (170-180 minutes after egg laying).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0089570</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005319 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005319">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005259"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00018001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005317"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005318"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Stage 7 begins when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Invagination of the anterior and posterior midgut and hindgut follows. The &apos;discoid plate&apos; that carries the pole cells forms a pocket. Transverse furrows (dorsal folds) form on the dorsal surface. This stage ends when the anterior wall of the amnioproctodeal invagination starts moving anteriorly and the pole cells are no longer visible externally. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (180-190 minutes after egg laying).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>FlyBase_development_CV</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBdv:00005319</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Temporal ordering number - 240.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>embryonic stage 7</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005319"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Stage 7 begins when the pole cells have adopted a dorsal (horizontal) position at the posterior. Invagination of the anterior and posterior midgut and hindgut follows. The &apos;discoid plate&apos; that carries the pole cells forms a pocket. Transverse furrows (dorsal folds) form on the dorsal surface. This stage ends when the anterior wall of the amnioproctodeal invagination starts moving anteriorly and the pole cells are no longer visible externally. Duration at 25 degrees C: approximately 10 minutes (180-190 minutes after egg laying).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0089570</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005321 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBdv_00005321">
